# Skill-First Policy for This Repo

Before executing **any** benchmark, cluster lifecycle, load-test, or advisor task — including teardown, cleanup, and status checks — **read and follow the relevant skill file** under `.cursor/skills/`.

Do **not** quote a script command or shell one-liner as a substitute for invoking the skill. The skill is the source of truth for what steps, checks, and deliverables are required.

## Mapping common requests → skills

| User asks about… | Skill to invoke first |
|---|---|
| Load-test deploy / run / teardown / status | `benchmark-load-test` |
| Autoscaling advisor / recommendations | `autoscaling-advisor` |
| AutoNode / Karpenter cluster provisioning | `benchmark-create-hcp-autonode` |
| Cluster install timing (Classic or HCP) | `benchmark-cluster-install` |
| CAS scale-up / scale-down | `benchmark-autoscale-up` / `benchmark-autoscale-down` |
| HPA benchmark | `benchmark-hpa` |
| HPA → CAS cascade | `benchmark-hpa-triggers-cas` |
| Karpenter progressive scale | `benchmark-autonode-scale` |
| CAS progressive scale | `benchmark-cas-scale` |
| Parallel node provisioning | `benchmark-parallel-nodes` |
| Surge / spike scenarios | `benchmark-planned-surge` / `benchmark-sudden-spike` |
| Overprovisioning / balloon pods | `benchmark-overprovisioning` |
| Spot instances | `benchmark-spot-instances` |
| ARM64 / Graviton nodes | `benchmark-arm-nodes` |
| Full suite (tests 01–09) | `benchmark-run-all` |
| Advanced suite (tests 10–16) | `benchmark-advanced-autoscaling` |
| ROSA CLI syntax / cluster ops | `rosa-cli` |
